ns i ✓ ✓ ✓ Automation integrations (IFTTT, Zapier) i ✓ ✓ Email & SMS journaling i ✓ ✓ Strava integration ✓ ✓ Browser extensions & shortcuts i ✓ ✓ ✓ Organization Keep entries organized with tags, favorites, and search. Feature Basic Silver Gold Unlimited journals ✓ ✓ ✓ Collections ✓ ✓ Tags, search & filters ✓ ✓ ✓ Calendar, Map & Media views ✓ ✓ ✓ Privacy & Security Protect entries with encryption, passcode, and secure backup. Feature Basic Silver Gold End-to-end encryption ✓ ✓ ✓ Passcode protection ✓ ✓ ✓ Biometric lock ✓ ✓ ✓ Secure cloud backup ✓ ✓ ✓ Sync & Access Write anywhere with seamless sync across devices and apps. Feature Basic Silver Gold Device access 1 device Unlimited devices Unlimited devices Web access ✓ ✓ ✓ Sharing Journal together with family, friends, or small groups in a private, secure place. Feature Basic Silver Gold Shared Journals i ✓ ✓ ✓ Preservation & Export Export, back up, or turn entries into lasting hardcover or paperback printed books. Feature Basic Silver Gold Book printing discount 25% off 35% off Export to PDF ✓ ✓ ✓ Data export (CSV/JSON) ✓ ✓ ✓ AI & Innovation Optional tools that support deeper reflection through chat, personalized prompts, and summaries. Feature Basic Silver Gold Daily Chat ✓ Go Deeper Prompts ✓ Entry Summaries ✓ Title Suggestions ✓ Image Generation ✓ Apple Intelligence Features i ✓ Day One Labs ✓ ✓ Capture life’s moments, anytime, anywhere. Download the free Day One journal app on iPhone, Android, iPad, Mac, and Apple Watch. Or access your Day One Journal from any browser. App Store Android Mac Login now FAQs Is there a free version of Day One?Yes. Day One includes a free plan with unlimited text entries and journals, daily prompts, search, and end-to-end encryption. You can start journaling by downloading Day One. What’s the difference between Basic, Silver, and Gold?Basic includes everything you need to start journaling.Silver expands your experience with additional media, sync, and integrations.Gold adds advanced features designed for deeper reflection and long-term memory keeping. Can I try Silver or Gold before subscribing?Yes. You can start a free trial of a paid plan before committing. If you cancel before the trial ends, you won’t be charged. Please note: free trial eligibility is controlled by the App Stores. If you’ve already used a Day One free trial (for example, Silver), the App Store may not allow another free trial when upgrading to Gold. How do I upgrade my plan?You can upgrade at any time from within the app on the platform where you originally subscribed. I subscribed on iPhone. Can I upgrade on the web or Android?Upgrades and billing changes must be made on the platform where you originally subscribed (Apple, Google, etc.). If you’re unsure, our support team can help you find the right place to manage your plan. What happens if I downgrade?You’ll keep access to your entries. Features included in higher tiers may become limited, but your content remains safe and accessible. Will I lose my journal if I cancel?No. Your entries remain yours. If you cancel a paid plan, you’ll revert to the free version with access to your journal, subject to free plan limits. Can I switch between Silver and Gold later?Yes. You can upgrade or downgrade between paid plans as your needs change. Are there any limits to the AI features?Day One’s AI features have daily usage limits to ensure fair access for all users. If you reach the limit, you’ll see a message letting you know. Have more questions? Check out our help page or contact us. Capture life’s moments, anytime, anywhere. Download the free Day One journal app for free on iPhone, Android, iPad, Mac, and Apple Watch. Or access your Day One Journal from any browser. App Store Android Mac Login Now Notifications Search resultsLoading popular results…FiltersShow filtersSort by: Relevance•Newest•OldestFilter options Close SearchSearch powered by Jetpack
